<title>NETHERLANDS: Philips to end Little Rock lamp production.</title>
<headline>Philips to end Little Rock lamp production.</headline>
<dateline>EINDHOVEN, Netherlands 1996-12-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Philips Electronics NV said on Wednesday it would phase out production of incandescent lamps at Little Rock, Arkansas, over the next two years.  </p>
<p>Philips said the gradual phasing out of the Little Rock lamp manufacturing plant was part of Philips Lighting's ongoing effort to increase efficiency.</p>
<p>The plant, bought from Westinghouse Electric Co. in 1983, employs some 480 people.</p>
